ork  well maybe the last time life threw you  a curveball did you handle it in a way  that you were proud of or like me maybe  did you start getting frustrated more  easily and lash out at your coworkers on  occasion these are the sorts of things  that show whether we're emotionally fit  or not and most of us myself included  making a lot of improvement but how do  we become emotionally fit well I would  first recommend you check out some talks  from dr. Emily on hall she's given some  really excellent presentations on this  subject but for now I want to recommend  one really easy thing you can do would  you simply find a couple hours a week to  play and what I mean by play is engaged  in something purely for enjoyment rather  than any practical purpose  all right maybe put together a puzzle  with a loved one start writing that  fanfic finally or pick up an old hobby  right and probably step away from the  computer for a little while that it's  easy for us to think we're relaxing when  really we're still working in some  capacity right which is why I say that  we need to play and not that we need to  relax playing  has been found to reduce stress it  builds better relationships between  those involved in it and it enables you  to respond better when things go wrong  now if you're unsure how do you  intelectual Ian gauged in a playful  activity there's a simple litmus test  you can use which is inspired by this  quote from Niall Horan here's a member  of the boy band One Direction actually  [Music]  he once said when someone asked him why  he wanted to play the guitar more  someone told me in a smile on my face  gets bigger when I play the guitar so my  question for you all today is what makes  you smile more find that and do it try  to do it for at least a couple hours a  week now obviously don't turn it into an  obligation but it will be tremendously  beneficial becoming emotionally fit is  an ongoing process  ongoing commitment but it's one that's  going to help u